INFRA-QT-DEPLOY-001 -- both guards made to fail on the real defect
generated 2026-09-26 20:17:53

A guard that cannot fire proves nothing, so the collision is recreated:
one empty directory, %LOCALAPPDATA%\bettercad-aaa, nothing else changed.

--- configure, with the collision present ---
  CMake Error at cmake/BetterCADBuildLocation.cmake:192 (message):
    The dependency prefix is not what its own 8.3 short name leads to, so the
    Qt runtime cannot be deployed: 'bettercad-aaa' is reached instead of
    'bettercad-deps'.
  
      dependencies:      C:/Users/uqhas/AppData/Local/bettercad-deps
      reached instead:   C:/Users/uqhas/AppData/Local/bettercad-aaa
      short name of the dependency prefix: C:/Users/uqhas/AppData/Local/BETTER~1
  
    The first six characters of these two names are the same once the
    characters illegal in an 8.3 name are removed, so both answer to that short
    name, and a lookup that enumerates the parent takes the first of them in
    name order.  windeployqt resolves the Qt binary directory that way, and
    then reports that it cannot find Qt6Core.dll under a path nobody
    configured.

